### Saga scenarios — VS Code "REST Client" or IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### {{$guid}} creates a new Idempotency-Key per request; replace it with a fixed value to test replays.

@transfers = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/transfers
@core = http://localhost:8081/core/v1

### 1. Own bank transfer → COMPLETED
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-own-bank

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"2000000001","holderName":"Carlos Vega"},
 "amount":100.00,"currency":"USD","concept":"Rent"}

### 2. Instant interbank transfer (RPI) → COMPLETED
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"010","accountNumber":"3000000001","holderName":"Pedro Mora"},
 "amount":50.00,"currency":"USD","concept":"Dinner"}

### 3. Deferred interbank transfer (SPI) → COMPLETED after ~3 s
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"099","accountNumber":"3000000002","holderName":"Lucia Paz"},
 "amount":25.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 4. Insufficient funds → REJECTED
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-200","sourceAccount":"1000000002",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"2000000001","holderName":"Carlos Vega"},
 "amount":500.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 5. Blocked source account → REJECTED
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-300","sourceAccount":"1000000003",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"2000000001","holderName":"Carlos Vega"},
 "amount":10.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 6. Credit to a closed account → REVERSED (compensation)
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"2000000002","holderName":"Sofia Leon"},
 "amount":40.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 7. Clearing rejects AC01 → REVERSED (compensation)
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"010","accountNumber":"3000000000","holderName":"Nobody"},
 "amount":30.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 8. Lost payment order → FAILED after ~45 s (manual reconciliation)
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"010","accountNumber":"3000007777","holderName":"Lost"},
 "amount":5.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 9. Fraud engine denies → REJECTED
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"9999999999","holderName":"Suspicious"},
 "amount":10.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 10a. Idempotency: send this twice → same transferId, second one with Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: fixed-key-0001

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"2000000001","holderName":"Carlos Vega"},
 "amount":1.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 10b. Same key, different payload → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: fixed-key-0001

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"1000000001",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"001","accountNumber":"2000000001","holderName":"Carlos Vega"},
 "amount":2.00,"currency":"USD"}

### 11. Validation → 400 problem details
POST {{transfers}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{"customerId":"C-100","sourceAccount":"123",
 "beneficiary":{"bankCode":"1","accountNumber":"2000000001","holderName":"Carlos Vega"},
 "amount":-5,"currency":"USD"}

### Follow a transfer (paste the transferId)
GET {{transfers}}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Balances
GET {{core}}/accounts/1000000001

###
GET {{core}}/accounts/2000000001

### Chaos: half of the postings apply and then answer 503 (unknown outcome)
PUT {{core}}/admin/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{"failureRate":0.5,"mode":"AFTER_APPLY"}

### Chaos off
PUT {{core}}/admin/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{"failureRate":0,"mode":"BEFORE_APPLY"}
